+# P5 desk props v2 — generation notes
+
+All outputs are 1536×1024 PNG with a transparent canvas (alpha sampled after delivery). Built-in image generation was used; the master desk was a style, light, and perspective reference and the old asset was a subject reference.
+
+## letters.png
+
+**Full prompt**
+
+```text
+Premium cinematic painted 3D-cartoon illustration, same world and finish as the reference desk; one consistent light setup — warm oil-lamp key light from the desk, cool moonlit rim from a back window; soft volumetric light, gentle bloom on highlights, shallow depth of field, rich smooth gradients with fine film grain and no banding; consistent perspective and scale across frames; restrained, handcrafted, studio-quality game-art polish.
+
+Use case: stylized-concept
+Asset type: high-resolution isolated desk-prop game asset
+Primary request: Repaint the subject of the supplied letters-many reference: a single neat stack of several sealed parchment letters/envelopes, tied together with thin natural twine and topped by one small dark-red wax seal. The envelopes are aged cream parchment with folded triangular flaps, subtle deckled edges and warm handmade fibers; the wax seal has no emblem or legible mark.
+Input images: Image #1 master desk, world/finish/lighting/perspective reference only; Image #2 old letters prop, subject reference only.
+Scene/backdrop: genuinely transparent background, no backdrop.
+Composition/framing: landscape 3:2, at least 1536×1024 pixels; one isolated object only, same slightly-high three-quarter angle as the master desk, object fills about 82% of frame width, fully inside the frame with generous transparent margins.
+Lighting/mood: warm oil-lamp key from right, cool rim from behind.
+Constraints: true alpha transparency; no floor, no ground contact shadow, no vignette; no other objects; no Clepsydra, person, figure, face, hand, statue, UI, badge, logo, watermark, modern objects, neon, purple-cyan.
+Text: none. Absolutely no legible text, letters, numerals, glyphs, symbols, insignia, or writing; any paper detail must be only illegible non-semantic texture.
+```
+
+Output: 1536×1024; transparent.
+
+Honest note: The envelope stack is considerably more detailed and close-up than the small legacy icon, and the transparent-preview lighting includes conspicuous warm/cool glow around the silhouette.
+
+## tablet.png
+
+**Full prompt**
+
+```text
+Premium cinematic painted 3D-cartoon illustration, same world and finish as the reference desk; one consistent light setup — warm oil-lamp key light from the desk, cool moonlit rim from a back window; soft volumetric light, gentle bloom on highlights, shallow depth of field, rich smooth gradients with fine film grain and no banding; consistent perspective and scale across frames; restrained, handcrafted, studio-quality game-art polish.
+
+Use case: stylized-concept
+Asset type: high-resolution isolated desk-prop game asset
+Primary request: Repaint the subject of the supplied tablet-half reference: one small ancient rectangular writing tablet, landscape orientation, a thick dark walnut wooden frame with softly worn beveled edges and a recessed dark charcoal-brown beeswax writing surface. The wax surface bears only faint irregular scrape marks and non-semantic, entirely illegible texture—no writing.
+Input images: Image #1 master desk, world/finish/lighting/perspective reference only; Image #3 old tablet prop, subject reference only.
+Scene/backdrop: genuinely transparent background, no backdrop.
+Composition/framing: landscape 3:2, at least 1536×1024 pixels; one isolated object only, same slightly-high three-quarter angle as the master desk, object fills about 82% of frame width, fully inside the frame with generous transparent margins.
+Lighting/mood: warm oil-lamp key from right, cool rim from behind.
+Constraints: true alpha transparency; no floor, no ground contact shadow, no vignette; no other objects; no Clepsydra, person, figure, face, hand, statue, UI, badge, logo, watermark, modern objects, neon, purple-cyan.
+Text: none. Absolutely no legible text, letters, numerals, glyphs, symbols, insignia, or writing on the wax or wood.
+```
+
+Output: 1536×1024; transparent.
+
+Honest note: The frame is especially thick and heavily weathered; it may read more rustic than the smaller, tidier legacy tablet.
+
